\frametitle{The two core filters in code}
\begin{lstlisting}[language=Python]
import cv2
gauss  = cv2.GaussianBlur(noisy, (5,5), 0)   # grain / Gaussian noise
median = cv2.medianBlur(noisy, 3)            # salt-and-pepper specks

# diagnose first: peek at a flat patch
patch = noisy[y:y+15, x:x+15]
print(patch.std())   # wide spread -> Gaussian; 0/255 spikes -> impulse
\end{lstlisting}
  \begin{infobox}
    Try median first for specks; averaging/Gaussian for grain. Measure, don't guess — Session 2 shows how (PSNR/SSIM).
  \end{infobox}
